## Player Performance Plot
```python
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

# Sample data
players = ['Player 1', 'Player 2', 'Player 3', 'Player 4', 'Player 5']
average_points_scored = [15.6, 12.1, 10.9, 9.5, 8.2]

plt.bar(players, average_points_scored)
plt.xlabel('Player')
plt.ylabel('Average Points Scored')
plt.title('Player Performance')
plt.show()
```
This plot visualizes the player performance, making it easier to compare the top players.

